Task 1 - Retail Sales Analysis
Project Overview
This project performs Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) on a Retail Sales and Customer Demographics dataset.

The objective is to analyze customer purchasing behavior, product category performance, gender-wise sales, and monthly sales trends using Python.

Dataset
The dataset contains 1,000 retail transactions and 9 columns:

Transaction ID
Date
Customer ID
Gender
Age
Product Category
Quantity
Price per Unit
Total Amount
Tools & Technologies
Python
Pandas
NumPy
Matplotlib
Seaborn
Jupyter Notebook
Analysis Performed
The following analysis was performed:

Loaded and inspected the dataset
Checked data types
Converted the Date column into datetime format
Checked for missing values
Checked for duplicate records
Created customer age groups
Analyzed sales by product category
Analyzed sales by gender
Analyzed monthly sales trends
Created visualizations to understand the data
Key Business Insights
Highest-selling category: Electronics — 156,905
Highest sales by gender: Female — 232,840
Best sales month: May 2023 — 53,150
Average transaction value: 456.00
Average customer age: 41.4 years
Average quantity per transaction: 2.51 units
Conclusion
The analysis shows that Electronics generated the highest sales among the three product categories. Female customers contributed slightly more to total sales than male customers. May 2023 recorded the highest monthly sales during the analyzed period.

Overall, the EDA provides useful insights into customer demographics, product performance, and sales trends that can support retail business decision-making.

